{
  "rule_id": "R44_66",
  "target": "ts",
  "tier": "T2",
  "governed_construct": "A module-level export of a value (component, function, class, constant) from a source file: every ExportNamedDeclaration, re-export (export {..} from / export * from), and every default export form (export default <declaration|expression>, export { x as default }).",
  "interpretation": "The rule asks that a file expose its components and utilities through named exports rather than a default export. A file with at least one export where none is a default export is SATISFIED (export function/const/class/let, export { a, b }, export { x } from, export * from, export type all conform). Any default export makes the file VIOLATED, including export default function/class/arrow/identifier and the aliased form export { x as default }, even if other named exports are also present. A file with no export statements at all (a script or entry point) is NOT_APPLICABLE. Text that merely mentions 'export default' inside comments or string/template literals is not an export and does not count.",
  "fixtures": [
    {
